Problem: We define the sequence \( a_{0}, a_{1}, \ldots \) starting from an arbitrary value \( a_{0} \) using the recursion formula \( a_{n+1} = \sin a_{n} \). Does this sequence converge, and if so, what is its limit?

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
